  "body": "Add a troubleshooting page to the guide, organised by **what the user sees** rather than by rule (`guide/refusals.md` explains the rules; this page answers \"I got this message, now what?\").\n\nFor each entry:\n- the message as the app shows it (or its stable start, for messages that name an operation or a value);\n- what it means in plain words;\n- the usual causes;\n- the fix, step by step, with the setting to change and where it is.\n\nStart with the refusals and problems users meet most. Pull them from the refusal strings in the code (posting, verify, gouge and collision, holder and workholding, reach and travel, fidelity) and from recent user-reported issues. Also cover a few non-refusal problems: the app won't start or shows a blank window (GPU, #74), a model imports at the wrong scale, an operation stays Stale, or a post writes nothing.\n\nKeep the message text in sync: a later PR that changes a listed message should update the page. A test that checks each listed message stem still exists in the source would catch drift cheaply.\n\nDone means: a troubleshooting page with at least 20 entries covering posting, verify, setups, tools and import, each with message, meaning, cause and fix, linked from refusals.md and the guide index.\n",
